      "claim": "In fasted healthy subjects, propranolol, a lipophilic basic secondary amine with a basic pKa near 9.5 similar to the query's ionization profile, has absolute oral bioavailability 27.2%, above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C10","C25"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Metoprolol, a lipophilic basic secondary amine bearing a methoxyphenyl group, shows systemic availability 84% in cirrhosis (78 +/- 12% excluding portocaval anastomosis), supporting high F for this structural class.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C15","C22","C30","C31"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Diphenhydramine, a lipophilic basic amine, has systemic availability 0.69 after oral dosing in fasted healthy volunteers.",
      "card_ids": ["C13","C33"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Verapamil, a lipophilic basic amine with a dimethoxyphenyl group, has absolute F 52.3% in cirrhosis; the lowest visible verapamil record is 22%, still above 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C05","C06","C19","C43","C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 human absorption records show that lipophilic basic amines with similar ionization profiles (propranolol >90%, metoprolol ~100%, alprenolol 93-96%) are almost completely absorbed in humans, supporting the absorption component of oral bioavailability for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C64","C60","C66","C63","C61","C58"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63","C64","C65","C66","C67"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "L4 records are human fraction absorbed, not absolute F; they do not quantify first-pass metabolism or systemic availability.",
    "The query's very low neutral fraction (0.01) at pH 7.4 could reduce passive permeability, but propranolol/metoprolol/alprenolol with similar basic pKa show high absorption; no direct query permeability data.",
    "First-pass metabolic clearance for the query is unknown; L1/L2 analogs with first-pass liability still exceed 20% (propranolol 27.2%, verapamil 22-52%).",
    "Most high-F records come from cirrhosis or modified-release conditions; fasted healthy analogs are limited to propranolol and diphenhydramine."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because all visible records report F values >=22% for structurally similar lipophilic basic amines (propranolol 27.2% fasted, metoprolol 84% cirrhosis, diphenhydramine 69% fasted, verapamil 22-52%), and L4 human absorption records show near-complete absorption for similar basic amines (propranolol >90%, metoprolol ~100%, alprenolol 93-96%). No affirmative evidence supports F < 20%. Confidence remains moderate because transfer is indirect and no direct query F is available."
}

